\hline\(y=2 x+3\) & -1 & 7 \\
\hline
\end{tabular}

From Fig. 2.1, you can see that the graph of \(y=2 x+3\) intersects the \(x\)-axis mid-way between \(x=-1\) and \(x=-2\), that is, at the point \(\left(-\frac{3}{2}, 0\right)\). You also know that the zero of \(2 x+3\) is \(-\frac{3}{2}\). Thus, the zero of the polynomial \(2 x+3\) is the \(x\)-coordinate of the point where the graph of \(y=2 x+3\) intersects the

