Therefore,
\[\mathrm{PQ}=\sqrt{\left(x_{2}-x_{1}\right)^{2}+\left(y_{2}-y_{1}\right)^{2}}\]

Note that since distance is always non-negative, we take only the positive square root. So, the distance between the points \(\mathrm{P}\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\right)\) and \(\mathrm{Q}\left(x_{2}, y_{2}\right)\) is
\[\mathbf{P Q}=\sqrt{\left(x_{2}-x_{1}\right)^{2}+\left(y_{2}-y_{1}\right)^{2}},\]
which is called the distance formula.

