Section 7.3 discusses the Section Formula for the coordinates \((x, y)\) of a point P which divides internally the line segment joining the points \(\mathrm{A}\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\right)\) and \(\mathrm{B}\left(x_{2}, y_{2}\right)\) in the ratio \(m_{1}: m_{2}\) as follows:
\[x=\frac{m_{1} x_{2}+m_{2} x_{1}}{m_{1}+m_{2}}, \quad y=\frac{m_{1} y_{2}+m_{2} y_{1}}{m_{1}+m_{2}}\]

Note that, here, \(\mathrm{PA}: \mathrm{PB}=m_{1}: m_{2}\).
However, if P does not lie between A and B but lies on the line AB , outside the line segment AB , and \(\mathrm{PA}: \mathrm{PB}=m_{1}: m_{2}\), we say that P divides externally the line segment joining the points A and B . You will study Section Formula for such case in higher classes.

