\subsection*{8.5 Summary}

In this chapter, you have studied the following points :
1. In a right triangle ABC , right-angled at B , \(\sin \mathrm{A}=\frac{\text { side opposite to angle } \mathrm{A}}{\text { hypotenuse }}, \cos \mathrm{A}=\frac{\text { side adjacent to angle } \mathrm{A}}{\text { hypotenuse }} \tan \mathrm{A}=\frac{\text { side opposite to angle } \mathrm{A}}{\text { side adjacent to angle } \mathrm{A}}\).
2. \(\operatorname{cosec} \mathrm{A}=\frac{1}{\sin \mathrm{~A}} ; \sec \mathrm{A}=\frac{1}{\cos \mathrm{~A}} ; \tan \mathrm{A}=\frac{1}{\cot \mathrm{~A}}, \tan \mathrm{~A}=\frac{\sin \mathrm{A}}{\cos \mathrm{A}}\).
3. If one of the trigonometric ratios of an acute angle is known, the remaining trigonometric ratios of the angle can be easily determined.
4. The values of trigonometric ratios for angles \(0^{\circ}, 30^{\circ}, 45^{\circ}, 60^{\circ}\) and \(90^{\circ}\).
5. The value of \(\sin \mathrm{A}\) or \(\cos \mathrm{A}\) never exceeds 1 , whereas the value of \(\sec \mathrm{A}\left(0^{\circ} \leq \mathrm{A}<90^{\circ}\right)\) or \(\operatorname{cosec} \mathrm{A}\left(0^{\circ}<\mathrm{A} \leq 90^{\circ}\right)\) is always greater than or equal to 1 .
6. \(\sin ^{2} \mathrm{~A}+\cos ^{2} \mathrm{~A}=1\),
\(\sec ^{2} \mathrm{~A}-\tan ^{2} \mathrm{~A}=1\) for \(0^{\circ} \leq \mathrm{A}<90^{\circ}\),
\(\operatorname{cosec}^{2} \mathrm{~A}=1+\cot ^{2} \mathrm{~A}\) for \(0^{\circ}<\mathrm{A} \leq 90^{\circ}\).

