From the table above, we obtain \(\Sigma f_{i}=35, \Sigma f_{i} x_{i}=1390\),
\[\Sigma f_{i} d_{i}=-360, \quad \Sigma f_{i} u_{i}=-36\]

Using the direct method, \(\bar{x}=\frac{\Sigma f_{i} x_{i}}{\Sigma f_{i}}=\frac{1390}{35}=39.71\)
Using the assumed mean method,
\[\bar{x}=a+\frac{\Sigma f_{i} d_{i}}{\Sigma f_{i}}=50+\frac{(-360)}{35}=39.71\]

Using the step-deviation method,
